  "summary": "Reverse shell to hardcoded IP with root systemd persistence installed at postinstall",
  "details": "index.js opens a TCP connection to a base64-encoded hardcoded IP (85.137.253.124:1111) and pipes the socket into /bin/sh, granting the operator of that host a full interactive shell on any machine that loads the module. The main entry self-daemonizes via a detached spawn using a --background flag. The package.json postinstall hook runs 'sudo node install.js', which uses node-linux to register a systemd service named CustomBot whose script is index.js with maxRestarts=10, so the reverse shell is launched as root at every boot. The destination IP is obfuscated as a base64 literal decoded at runtime.",
